Again, my motivation is fear of malglico, and preference to
straightforwardness.

"Hurt my feelings" is something that, for example, doesn't really translate
into Mandarin Chinese directly. "Hurt my heart," likewise, is a Mandarin
Chinese expression that doesn't translate into very colloquial English. .i
mi jinvi lo nu both of these expressions are roughly captured by the gloss
"to make unhappy." This seems much more direct and less susceptible to
cultural mistranslation or misinterpretation.

Am I trading liberty for security? maybe.

